          "path": "_m/9/q/k/z/death-valley-extremes-wk/borax-museum-construct.jpg",
          "filename": "Borax Museum, Death Valley, California.jpg",
          "caption": "Borax Museum was constructed in 1883 by Francis \"Borax\" Smith, founder of the Pacific Coast Borax Company. The oldest house in Death Valley, it originally stood in 20-Mule Team Canyon where it served as an office, bunk house, and ore-checking station for miners at the Monte Blanco deposits. In 1954 the building was moved to Furnace Creek Ranch to serve as a museum. As of 2026, it is still used as a museum.",
